    "source_text": "Following general procedure F using 4k (90 mg, 0.25 mmol), B2pin2 (127 mg, 0.50 mmol), [Ir(COD)OMe]2 (2.5 mg, 0.00375 mmol) and 1a (3.8 mg, 0.0075 mmol) in THF (1.25 mL). Stirred in vial at 70 °C for 20 hours. Analysis of crude 1 H NMR using internal standard 1,2‐dimethoxyethane showed ~14:1 meta:para borylation in 99% yield (these numbers include the meta/para products which have also undergone NH borylation at the higher temperature).  The crude product was purified by silica gel chromatography (10% EtOAc in Petroleum Ether 40‐60 o C) which resulted in the cleavage of the N‐ B bond of the NH‐borylation products and gave the title compound (as a 15.2:1 mixture of meta:para ratio, as determined by 1 H NMR) as a yellowish oil (113 mg, 0.23 mmol, 93%).",
    "text_sha256": "92308ac93bc8e1b83ffb36bec484b989ed7ce4697bbfe26d9422d164e6a000be",
